1. Claim 15 (Currently amended): A method for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, __wherein the information is added by a media request broker that analyzes server load, latency, and geographic proximity data__;
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, __wherein the selection is performed by the media request broker in response to an http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and wherein the media request broker is a distinct entity separate from both the client computer and the server computers in the network path__.

2. Claim 16 (Currently amended): The method of claim 15, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, __wherein the media request broker receives the http request and determines server selection based on real-time server performance metrics__.

3. Claim 17 (Original): [Claim text not provided in application materials]

4. Claim 18 (Currently amended): The method of claim 17, the media request broker selecting the first server computer based on the information, __wherein the media request broker applies a selection algorithm that weighs at least two of the following factors: server load, network latency, geographic distance to the client computer, or server availability status__.

5. Claim 24 (Currently amended): A system for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the system comprising:
a client computer;
a plurality of server computers accessible through a network path;
a media request broker, __distinct from the client computer and server computers__, configured to:
receive information indicative of at least one server computer of a first set of one or more server computers;
add the information to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier;
select the first server computer based on the information, __wherein the selection is based on real-time analysis of server load, latency, and geographic proximity data, and wherein the media request broker processes http requests containing the unique signature identifying a media request__.

6. Claim 25 (Currently amended): The system of claim 24, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the system further comprising circuitry for selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, __wherein the media request broker circuitry receives and processes the http request to determine optimal server selection__.

7. Claim 27 (Currently amended): A computer program product for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the computer program product comprising:
a computer-readable medium;
program instructions stored on the medium, the instructions configured to:
access a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
add information indicative of at least one server computer of a first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier;
select the first server computer based on the information, __wherein the program instructions implement a media request broker function that analyzes server performance metrics and generates server selection decisions based on real-time data__.

8. Claim 28 (Currently amended): The computer program product of claim 27, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the computer program product further comprising the program step of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, __wherein the program instructions further comprise steps for the media request broker to receive the http request and execute a server selection algorithm based on multiple performance factors__.
